# STATICS — the non-learned baseline family on the training panel

Workspace `/home/sat/mcrl-v025-rank-ws`. Interpreter
`/home/sat/mcrl-leo-handover/.venv/bin/python` only. **Never modify**
`/home/sat/mcrl-leo-handover` or its `.venv`. **Design-phase measurement, not a claim.**

**Resource limits, enforced.** Load hit 157 with 0 GB free twice today. **Hard cap: 3 python
processes, `nice -n 15`, all BLAS threads = 1, peak RSS under 5 GB per process.** Print a
peak-RSS line and an `anchor k/N` progress line. **Three training runs and eight jobs are
live** — read only from their directories, write only into your own.

## Why

A sibling project's win bar was *"beat plain shared-Q + a **weak static**"*, with the strong
static held as the teacher/ceiling and **explicitly dropped as a comparison-to-win**. Its most
consequential measurement was not that the learned method underperformed — it was that the
learned method **lost to `round_robin`**, and that a collapsed policy is **worse than random**,
because the environment punishes crowding superlinearly.

This project has a strong static already measured on its training panel
(`TRAINING-PANEL-CEILINGS-2026-09-10.md`, `/home/sat/mcrl-v025-ceiling30-ws`) and one weak
static (the geometric nearest-eligible base). **It has no round-robin, no load-balancing
heuristic, no myopic greedy, and no random floor.** Without those, "the learned proposal is
worth something" cannot be stated at all.

## What to measure

On the **same 12-anchor training panel**, with **exactly the construction `PANELCEIL` used** —
same anchors, same guard, same tie-break, same corrected provisioning, same realised 48-boundary
pooling, **declared full-buffer numerator, no demand cap** (declaration v1.8 item 5) — evaluate
this family. **Define each precisely in the report before giving its number; do not assume I
know what you implemented.**

| arm | what it is |
|---|---|
| `RANDOM` | uniform over each user's legal options, a stated seed, **the absolute floor** |
| `ROUND_ROBIN` | a load-equalising assignment over legal options; state the exact rule |
| `RSS_MAX` | demand-blind greedy on best link quality — the classic weak static |
| `NEAREST_ELIGIBLE` | the geometric carrier base already measured at `11.027760`; **reproduce it as a parity check on your harness** |
| `MYOPIC_GREEDY` | one-step greedy on the declared objective using nominal physics, users in a stated order |
| `FIRST_IMPROVEMENT_FP` | the certified fixed point, `13.430253` — **strong static**, reproduce as the second parity check |

**The two parity checks matter more than the new arms.** If you cannot reproduce `11.027760`
and `13.430253` on your harness, stop and report that: every other number would be on a
different scale.

## Report per arm

- pooled EE (Mbit/J), pooled bits, pooled joules, on the declared numerator;
- **served PHY** and **rate-target attainment**;
- **`modal_frac`** (share of users on the single most-chosen beam), **`active`** (distinct beams
  and satellites), **`argmax_distinct`**;
- wall-clock per anchor, so the cheap arms' cost is on record.

Then one ordering table, cheapest to most expensive, with pooled EE beside it.

## What this is for, stated so the framing is not lost

The comparison structure this establishes is:

- **the weak-static family is the floor a learned proposal must clear** to be worth anything;
- **the strong static is the ceiling and is not a win target** — the owner has already said the
  system need not beat classical search;
- **random is the sanity floor**: a policy below it is not merely weak, it is crowding, and the
  environment punishes crowding superlinearly.

**Do not rank the learned arms here** — no learned checkpoint is read by this job. It produces
the reference scale that the learned numbers will later be placed against.

## Rules

- Separate **verified by running code**, **derived on paper**, **inferred**.
- Loss values are never evidence about EE. No learner is trained or scored here.
- Report every arm, including any that is worse than `RANDOM`. **Especially those.**
- Use development anchors only. **Do not read the 48 evaluation-only claim dates.**
- Change no sealed artefact.

